From d35fd2d7b3082027e0ed75b296c12a4a21e01dd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:39:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [libc] add cpu_set_t, CPU_* macros and
 sched_{set,get}affinity to sched.h

Frama-C\x27s share/libc/sched.h declares struct sched_param and the POSIX
scheduler functions, but none of glibc\x27s CPU-affinity interface
(cpu_set_t, CPU_SETSIZE, CPU_ZERO/SET/CLR/ISSET/COUNT/EQUAL/AND/OR/XOR
and their _S variants, CPU_ALLOC_SIZE, sched_setaffinity, and
sched_getaffinity). Linux code that pins processes or threads to CPUs
(such as nginx\x27s src/os/unix/ngx_setaffinity.h) therefore fails to parse.

Add the interface to share/libc/sched.h:
- __cpu_mask, __CPU_SETSIZE, __NCPUBITS, CPU_SETSIZE, and named
  struct __fc_cpu_set_t (typedef cpu_set_t) matching glibc\x27s layout
  (128 bytes on both x86_32 and x86_64);
- CPU_ZERO, CPU_SET, CPU_CLR, CPU_ISSET, CPU_COUNT, CPU_EQUAL, CPU_AND,
  CPU_OR, CPU_XOR, their _S forms, and CPU_ALLOC_SIZE, avoiding void *
  casts so WP\x27s Typed model accepts them and using &cpusetp->__bits[0]
  so dynamically sized sets (> 1024 CPUs) do not trigger out-of-bounds
  array-index alarms in Eva;
- __FC_EXTERN_FOR_MACRO(CPU_ZERO_S) __fc_cpu_zero_s for non-default
  setsize values, __sched_cpucount, sched_setaffinity, and
  sched_getaffinity with ACSL contracts (assigning errno as the rest of
  sched.h does, and initializing mask only on success in
  sched_getaffinity).

CPU_ALLOC / CPU_FREE (__sched_cpualloc / __sched_cpufree) are left out
for now as they allocate heap memory.

New test: tests/libc/sched_cpu_set.c (default x86_32 and -machdep
x86_64).
